00:33:49.794 --> 00:33:51.763 align:start size:84% position:16%
And one of the reasons
I gave at the time

00:33:51.763 --> 00:33:55.533 align:start size:88% position:13%
which is worth repeating
is that people,

00:33:55.533 --> 00:33:58.770
Trump might fail if
you put a whole bunch

00:33:58.770 --> 00:33:59.904
of attributes together.

00:33:59.904 --> 00:34:01.439
In other words his whole package

00:34:01.439 --> 00:34:03.641
might be inferior to
someone else or not,

00:34:03.641 --> 00:34:05.109
we can debate that.

00:34:05.109 --> 00:34:07.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if you use for example
a lexicographic rule.

00:34:07.412 --> 00:34:09.247 align:start size:81% position:19%
Lexicographic rule
basically says

00:34:09.247 --> 00:34:11.215
I look at my most
important attribute

00:34:11.215 --> 00:34:12.950
and I choose the one
that scores the best

00:34:12.950 --> 00:34:14.986 align:start size:84% position:16%
of that most
important attribute.

00:34:14.986 --> 00:34:16.788 align:start size:81% position:19%
Well if I use that
decision rule,

00:34:16.788 --> 00:34:18.089 align:start size:84% position:16%
there is an endless
number of ways

00:34:18.089 --> 00:34:19.390
